comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-06-25T17:37:16.724Z",codex-gpt5,"Implementation start: duplicate-safe all-status search found pm-rj3w as the only active telemetry worker reconnect item; related historical telemetry and Windows teardown items are closed or verification-gated. Scope is production worker reconnect/health hardening plus operator validation, not a new tracker item."
  "2026-06-25T17:41:04.644Z",codex-gpt5,"Investigation note: the concrete worker reconnect/healthcheck fix surface is scripts/prod/telemetry, which is intentionally git-ignored as private production operations material. I validated the needed local shape (Postgres reconnect after insert connection errors plus worker health state and stall warning), but will not force-add private ops files to a public PR. Releasing this item for a private deployment-path change."
  "2026-06-28T06:26:52.503Z",codex-gpt5,"Investigation note 2026-06-28: revisited during SDK/CLI continuation. Duplicate-safe all-status search still points to pm-rj3w as the canonical telemetry worker reconnect item. The concrete worker material remains under scripts/prod/telemetry as ignored/private production operations files, so it is intentionally not force-added to the public product PR; live telemetry/Sentry gates will still be verified as closeout evidence."
  "2026-07-12T06:14:58.724Z",maintainer-agent,"Second live occurrence 2026-07-12: pm-telemetry-postgres restarted ~04:00 (host maintenance window; container Up 8h vs worker Up 8d), worker logged continuous worker_insert_failed:the connection is closed, pm.telemetry.events backlogged to 111,382 messages / 1 consumer while Postgres kept serving reads. Remediation applied: docker compose restart telemetry-worker → consumer reattached, queue draining. This defect now has a repeatable operational cost on every Postgres restart — reconnect-with-backoff in the worker insert path remains the fix; consider raising priority."
  "2026-09-05T12:30:40.070Z","harness:codex","Live recurrence during PR 1199 closeout: the database stopped receiving events while the broker retained 1567 messages, including 200 unacknowledged deliveries. The running worker repeatedly reports a closed Postgres connection. Implementing the canonical reconnect owner in the private deployment surface, with a disposable real RabbitMQ/Postgres restart drill before deployment. Private operations files remain ignored; no production database restart is required."
  "2026-09-05T12:33:00.176Z","harness:codex","TDD negative control reproduced on disposable real services: original worker ingested 1 baseline row, then stayed at 1 instead of 21 after the fixture Postgres restart, while repeatedly reporting a closed connection. No production database was stopped. The same isolated test is now running against the reconnect candidate; it also verifies replay does not double-count daily aggregates."
  "2026-09-05T12:45:19.275Z","harness:codex","Private acceptance passed: 21 expected rows recover after the disposable Postgres restart with unchanged worker PID; replay leaves 23 valid unique events and 23 aggregate finishes. Two identical JSONB-incompatible events produce exactly one retained original JSON row with SQLSTATE 22P05, and a subsequent valid barrier event ingests. Readiness and the real stale watchdog exit also pass. Private worker digest fc68db96312f9529ee42d4f6acedba5c74272353756e2328c8d0ba475ee098b7. Public CI does not execute this private operational drill; its evidence is separate from the product coverage claim."
  "2026-09-05T12:46:34.942Z","harness:codex","Deployment verified on the private telemetry host using a worker-only rebuild with saved rollback baselines. The readiness check is healthy; broker and recent database receipts confirm recovery. The original poison event is retained separately rather than counted as a successfully ingested command. Source, drill, health override and runbook remain intentionally ignored; reviewed public tracker records contain aggregate evidence only."
  "2026-09-05T12:49:39.165Z","harness:codex","PR 1199 review-round closeout: full quality:static, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across 8444 tests, packed npm/Bun manual acceptance, package-artifact and docs-link gates pass. The latest pm-changelog package regenerated and verified CHANGELOG.md after structured closure. All active owners are released; the broader duplicate latency target remains open. Public source and private operational verification are recorded separately."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-05T12:45:20.836Z","harness:codex","Docker marks unhealthy containers but does not automatically restart them solely for failed health checks. The worker watchdog exits a stalled process; the existing unless-stopped restart policy supplies recovery. Reconnecting the consumer requeues unacknowledged events, and durable unique event IDs prevent replay from double-counting aggregates."
